Done — the dialog result is now consumed for a deterministic rebuild. `_MissingChannelKeyComposer` takes an `onKeyImported` callback, and the button handler awaits `showChannelKeyImportDialog` and invokes it when the result is true:

```dart
onPressed: () async {
  final imported = await showChannelKeyImportDialog(...);
  if (imported && context.mounted) onKeyImported();
},
```

The page passes `onKeyImported: () { if (mounted) setState(() {}); }`, so `_isMissingPrivateKey` is re-evaluated and the composer swaps immediately, independent of the session-notify relay. This also covers the edge called out in the thread: history reload fails silently after a successful import — the rebuild still happens because it is driven by the dialog result, not by the reload.

Covered by the reload-failure widget test in `test/network/ui_network_chat_page_test.dart` (key persisted, reload threw, composer swapped in) and the existing happy-path import test.

